---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = '';
---

<Layout title="Doppler Roller | James Welbes">
  <main class="case-study">

    <div class="hero">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <p class="eyebrow">Mobile App · Android · 2026</p>
        <h1>Doppler Roller</h1>
        <p class="lead">An Android app for generating scoped Doppler service tokens on demand, with masked display and one-tap clipboard copy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-img">
        <img src={base + '/img/built/doppler-roller-mockup.png'} alt="Doppler Roller app screenshot" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p>Doppler is great for managing secrets - but every time I needed a service token to hand off to an agent or script, I had to open the browser, log in to the Doppler dashboard, navigate to the right project and config, generate a token, and manually copy it. That's five or six steps for something I do constantly.</p>
      <p>On mobile it was even worse. The Doppler web UI is not built for quick phone access, and I wanted to be able to generate a fresh token and copy it in under ten seconds from anywhere.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>What it does</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Connects to your Doppler account with a personal API token stored securely on-device</li>
        <li>Lists all your projects and configs in dropdowns</li>
        <li>Generates a scoped read-only service token for the selected project/config with one tap</li>
        <li>Displays the token masked with asterisks - copy always gets the real value</li>
        <li>Tokens can be deleted from within the app when no longer needed</li>
        <li>Pull down to refresh the project list</li>
        <li>Settings screen for updating your API key or removing it entirely</li>
        <li>In-app update check: tap once, browser downloads the new APK, tap the notification to install</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>How it was built</h2>
      <p>Native Android app written in Kotlin. No frameworks, no React Native - just Kotlin, Material3 components, and OkHttp for the Doppler API calls. API keys are stored using Android's <code>EncryptedSharedPreferences</code>, which encrypts them at rest using AES-256.</p>

      <div class="tech-row">
        <span class="chip">Kotlin</span>
        <span class="chip">Android SDK</span>
        <span class="chip">Material3</span>
        <span class="chip">OkHttp</span>
        <span class="chip">Doppler API</span>
        <span class="chip">GitHub Releases</span>
        <span class="chip">EncryptedSharedPreferences</span>
      </div>

      <p>The update mechanism hits the GitHub releases API, compares version numbers, and opens the download URL in the browser. No Play Store, no Firebase - just a GitHub release and a browser download.</p>
      <p>The design system is dark navy with electric lime accents - <code>#0B111A</code> background, <code>#B5E851</code> primary. All custom drawables for buttons, inputs, and the token card.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Result</h2>
      <p>Generating a service token went from a five-step browser workflow to a two-tap process. It runs entirely on my phone with no server component. The token display is masked by default so I can use the app in public without exposing credentials.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="case-cta">
      <div class="cta-box rise">
        <h2>Have a problem like this?</h2>
        <p>Repetitive browser workflows, credential juggling, things you do ten times a day that deserve a dedicated tool. These are exactly the kind of things AI can knock out fast. If you've got a workflow that deserves a tool, let's talk.</p>
        <a href="/#audit" class="btn-accent">Let's talk →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .case-study { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 60px 24px 0; }
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 48px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 64px; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .eyebrow { font-size: .8rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem); font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 20px; line-height: 1.1; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }
  .hero-img img { width: 100%; border-radius: 16px; }
  .section { margin-bottom: 56px; }
  .section h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .section p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .section ul { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; padding-left: 20px; }
  .section ul li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .section code { background: var(--bg2); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: .9em; }
  .tech-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin: 20px 0; }
  .chip { font-size: .78rem; padding: 4px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; color: var(--muted); }
  .case-cta { padding: 72px 0 96px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line2); }
  .cta-box { background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(26,79,255,.12) 0%, rgba(26,79,255,.04) 100%); border: 1px solid rgba(26,79,255,.25); border-radius: 20px; padding: 48px; max-width: 680px; }
  .cta-box h2 { font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .cta-box p { color: var(--mut); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .btn-accent { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; }
  .btn-accent:hover { opacity: .88; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .cta-box { padding: 32px 24px; } }
</style>
